

🎨 Dashboard Color Protocol (DCP‑1.0)

A unified color‑severity‑event standard for distributed evolutionary telemetry systems.

1. Severity Levels (Canonical Set)

Every dashboard log event MUST declare a level.Levels are strictly ordered by operational urgency.

info — neutral system updates

success — confirmed positive outcomes

warning — non‑fatal anomalies or mitigations

error — validation failures or worker faults

critical — system‑threatening conditions

These levels form the backbone of the protocol.

2. Color Mapping (UI Rendering Contract)

Each severity level maps to a single canonical color.

