These colors are UI‑agnostic:HTML, terminal, and JS dashboards all follow the same mapping.

3. Event Types (Dashboard‑Visible Categories)

Every log packet MUST declare an event field.The dashboard recognizes the following event types:

log — general system messages

generation_update — evolution loop progress

simulation_frame — physics snapshot

mitigation_trigger — proactive safety action

checkpoint_saved — async persistence event

validation_error — schema or config failure

worker_fault — parallel process crash

Each event type has a default severity, but can be overridden.

4. Packet Schema (Strict Contract)

Every dashboard packet MUST follow this structure:

{
  "event": "log",
  "level": "warning",
  "color": "yellow",
  "message": "Mitigation triggered",
  "context": {
    "constraint": "thermal_load",
    "level": 2
  }
}

Required fields:

event — event category

level — severity

color — canonical color

message — human‑readable text

context — structured metadata (optional but recommended)

This schema is enforced by your validation layer.

5. Default Severity Rules

If a packet does not explicitly set a severity, the dashboard applies:

generation_update → info

simulation_frame → info

mitigation_trigger → warning

checkpoint_saved → success

validation_error → error

worker_fault → critical

This ensures consistent visual semantics across all nodes.

6. Dashboard Rendering Rules

The UI MUST:

render the color field as the primary visual indicator

display message prominently

show context as expandable metadata

group events by severity in the timeline

animate critical events (pulse or highlight)

persist error and critical events in a “sticky” alert bar

This turns the dashboard into a real‑time operational cockpit.

7. Non‑Negotiable Guarantees

The protocol guarantees:

deterministic color mapping

consistent severity semantics

schema‑validated packets

UI‑portable rendering

future extensibility (new event types allowed)

This is the foundation for a scalable, multi‑node telemetry ecosystem.

